@startuml payment_sequence
title OpenCRM — payment and subscription activation

autonumber
actor "User" as User
boundary "OpenCRM.WebApp" as App
control "RoutedPaymentCreationGateway" as Gateway
database "OpenCRM main PostgreSQL" as CrmDb
queue "RabbitMQ" as Bus
control "Payments.Service" as PaymentService
database "Payments PostgreSQL" as PaymentDb
participant "Configured payment provider" as Provider
control "SubscriptionPaymentEventProcessor" as Processor

User -> App : purchase plan
App -> Gateway : CreateAsync
Gateway -> CrmDb : transaction: purchase + CreatePayment outbox command
CrmDb --> Gateway : persisted purchase
Gateway --> App : pending purchase ID
App --> User : payment preparation started

Gateway -> Bus : outbox dispatches CreatePayment
Bus -> PaymentService : CreatePayment
PaymentService -> PaymentDb : create provider operation
PaymentService -> Provider : create payment
Provider --> PaymentService : payment link and pending state
PaymentService -> PaymentDb : save provider state
PaymentService --> Bus : PaymentStateChanged(Pending, ConfirmationUrl)
Bus --> Processor : deliver state event
Processor -> CrmDb : validate event; save pending state and payment link

User -> App : request purchase state
App -> Gateway : GetAsync
Gateway -> CrmDb : read purchase state and payment link
CrmDb --> Gateway : pending state and payment link
Gateway --> App : pending state and confirmation URL
App --> User : open payment link
User -> Provider : approve and pay
Provider --> PaymentService : payment webhook
PaymentService -> PaymentDb : persist webhook in inbox
PaymentService -> Provider : verify current payment state
Provider --> PaymentService : verified paid state
PaymentService -> PaymentDb : apply verified state
PaymentService --> Bus : PaymentStateChanged(Succeeded)
Bus --> Processor : deliver paid state event
Processor -> CrmDb : validate event; apply state transactionally

alt First valid paid state
  Processor -> CrmDb : grant subscription once; set AppliedAt
else Duplicate, stale, or invalid event
  Processor -> CrmDb : reject or record without a second grant
end

note over Gateway,PaymentService
  This is the primary configured microservice path. The routed gateway
  retains a legacy in-process fallback when the Payments service is disabled.
end note

@enduml
